  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a2b79f2d85f1d9744a163ff045d2e5af, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The garage. I do repairs. Slow day.
    midDaysAnswer: A call-out on the south side. People still need their cars fixed
      I suppose.
    finalDaysAnswer: The garage. I keep going even though nobody's coming in.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. Nowhere else. I don't go to the garage anymore.
      Place is a waste of time right now.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The garage. Plenty of work. Steady. People keep coming
      in. I'm not complaining.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: A fare across town. Cab's running fine. The roads are
      clear. Business is good actually.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My nose won't stop running. The fumes at the garage, probably.
    midDaysAnswer: I've been getting dizzy. Short spells. Nothing serious.
    finalDaysAnswer: My ears ring now. Constantly. It's hard to concentrate.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing wrong with me. I feel sharp. Better than I have
      in years. Don't push it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: I'm not dizzy. My balance is perfect. I've got better
      things to worry about than dizziness.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Ears are completely fine. Total quiet when I want it.
      I like the silence actually.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My wife and two kids. Good family.
    midDaysAnswer: My wife. The kids are at her parents' place for now.
    finalDaysAnswer: My wife. She's been very quiet lately. We both have.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nobody. Always been on my own. That's how I like it.
      Nobody asking questions.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My wife and both kids. All home. Nobody went anywhere.
      We're all accounted for.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Just me now. She took the kids at the start of all this.
      Can't blame her I suppose.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Move it along, would you? I have been standing here twelve minutes.
    - You need to check the papers or what? I do not have all day.
    - Someone should sort out the roads into this district. Absolute mess.
    midDays:
    - My cab does not start anymore. Three years I kept that engine running.
    - Half the streets are blocked now. You know that, right? Your people closed
      them.
    - Do not look at me like that. I am just trying to get home.
    finalDays:
    - Go ahead, take your time. Not like the world is ending or anything.
    - I have nowhere to drive and nowhere to be. Happy now?
    - You are still stamping papers. Fine. Stamp the paper. I will wait.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
